From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:29:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): filter the sidebar to sessions that need you or
 changed recently

The sidebar lists every session and every project folder, so the few
sessions waiting on the viewer get lost. The status grouping can surface
them, but it is release-flagged and drops the project folders.

Add two device-local filters to the sessions filter menu, alongside the
My/Shared/All/Archived scope and independent of the grouping flag:

- "Needs me": sessions with a pending approval or unread agent output,
  using the same read-state as the unread dot.
- "Updated": Any time / Last 24 hours / Last 3 days / Last 7 days /
  Last 30 days. These are rolling windows, not calendar days, so the
  shortest one doesn't empty out just after midnight. The choices live
  in one ordered table, so another window is a one-line addition.

While either is on, project folders with nothing matching are hidden, the
filter icon is highlighted, and the open session stays listed. Pins are
unaffected, as with the scope filter.

Each active filter also shows as a chip beside the filter button (24h,
3d, 7d or 30d, and "Needs me"), so a short list reads as filtered at a
glance. A chip is a button that clears just its own filter; activated
from the keyboard, it hands focus back to the filter button.

Carried on custom until it lands upstream; cut from upstream/main as
feat/sidebar-attention-filters. Drop this copy once merged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 523c39f40ba01567b9f5d481c1a445139b6c0d1e)
